# zhao_forge_cliff_chain_fit_top -- HOLD PATH CLASSIFICATION
#
# DISTILLED AND COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. The full .hold.rpt is 1.4 MB and is
# GITIGNORED by the size rule, and CLAUDE.md records what happens then:
# 'the last attribution report is gone from disk and unreproducible'. This
# is the evidence for owner vacation directive 2026-09-23 section 6, so it
# is kept small and kept in git.
#
# THE QUESTION (named in design/fit_targets.yml BEFORE the fit ran): does the
# adopted evaluator still show a HOLD violation when its vdist read master is
# left as the composed console leaves it?
#
# THE ANSWER: yes, 200 violated paths -- and ALL 200 OF THEM LAUNCH FROM AN
# INPUT PIN. There is not ONE register-to-register hold violation in the
# design. Every launch point is a net that is INTERNAL in zhao_console_core:
#
#   lat_rsp_i      74 paths  <- {tcc_lat_wz, tcc_lat_wx, tcc_lat_h}, the compose
#                               cache's registered lattice outputs
#   serve_src_id_i 70 paths  <- terr_cc_serve_src_id_o. CHECKED RATHER THAN
#                               ASSUMED, because this one is not like the other
#                               four: that name IS a port of zhao_console_core.
#                               But it is an OUTPUT, a telemetry tap, and the
#                               net is DRIVEN INSIDE the core by
#                               zhao_terrain_compcache_front's serve_src_id_o.
#                               The path the feed sees is register-to-register
#                               within the core; the port observes it and does
#                               not source it.
#   t_ready_i      49 paths  <- u_forge_jobarb2.b_t_ready_o
#   v_ready_i       4 paths  <- u_forge_jobarb2.b_v_ready_o
#   o0_lat_req_i    3 paths  <- spd_c_lat_req, TERRAIN.SPDESC's request
#
# A virtual pin models almost no input delay, so data arrives too early
# relative to the clock and hold fails. Driven by a real registered source
# with real clock-to-out, these paths do not exist.
#
# Generated by hand from the ignored .hold.rpt; regenerate by re-running
# tools/quartus/run_block_fit.ps1 -Module zhao_forge_cliff_chain_fit_top.

